Spec: TenantInstallCmd

Purpose:
  Back the `agent tenant install` sub-command: resolve one @TenantInstance by namespace
    and name, publish it as the process-wide owner context and as the Rhai variable
    `instance`, inject the parsed CLI flags as the Rhai variable `args`, then hand the
    whole install work to the Rhai modules `context` and `install`. This file runs no
    install stage itself: no jukebox resolve, no download, no template render off
    `template_dir`, no `status` write — it only prepares the engine and hands off.
  Twin: near-clone of ./../service/install.sdd — an actual `diff` of the two source
    files shows exactly two deltas: the `use` line (@set_tenant/@TenantInstance over
    @set_service/@ServiceInstance, the same calls appearing at the identical call sites)
    and the `{script_dir}/tenant` search-dir segment; flags, snippet, the remaining
    three search directories and the step order are identical.

References:
  ./../service/install.sdd — the diff-verified twin; its open `[?]` tasks on the shared
    flag shape are mirrored here by cross-reference only.

Depends on:
  /common/src/rhaihandler.sdd — @Script::new resolver semantics and registration set,
    @Script::eval error lane, @Script::set_dynamic, @Script::ctx.
  /common/src/instancetenant.sdd — @TenantInstance and the @TenantInstance::get lookup
    this file awaits (attached by @impl_instance_common! per
    /common/src/instance_macros.sdd), and the registered bridges the scripts use for
    status writes.
  /common/src/context.sdd — @set_tenant store semantics and runtime preconditions.
  /common/src/lib.sdd — @common::Error variants, @common::Result and the
    @common::DEFAULT_AGENT_IMAGE default of `agent_image`.
  @clap @Args, @serde, @serde_json — flag parsing (flags, envs, defaults below) and the
    derives behind the `args` JSON.
  /agent/scripts/tenant/context.rhai and /agent/scripts/tenant/install.rhai — runtime
    handoff targets the snippet imports under the default `--script-dir`; owned instead
    by /agent/agent.sdd and unspecified here.
  ./mod.rs — the only caller: @context::init_k8s call, then this arm's
    `unwrap_or_else` error lane (tracing text and @process::exit(1), frozen by ./mod.sdd).

Exposes:
  @Parameters — clap @Args struct, also deriving @Debug, @Serialize and @Deserialize;
    mounted by @tenant::Commands::Install in ./mod.rs; all ten fields private to this
    module, reached only by the derive code and by this file.
  @run — @pub async fn @run(@args: @&@Parameters) -> @common::Result<@()>; the sole
    caller is @tenant::run (install dispatch arm).

Accepts:
  @Parameters.namespace — `-n` / `--namespace`, env `NAMESPACE`, value name `NAMESPACE`,
    @String, required (no `default_value`).
  @Parameters.instance — `-i` / `--instance`, env `INSTANCE`, value name `INSTANCE`,
    @String, required; names the CR to fetch and is never validated here.
  @Parameters.vynil_namespace — `-v` / `--vynil-namespace`, env `VYNIL_NAMESPACE`,
    value name `VYNIL_NAMESPACE`, @String, required; never read in this file beyond
    serialization into `args`.
  @Parameters.package_dir — `-p` / `--package-dir`, env `PACKAGE_DIRECTORY`, value name
    `PACKAGE_DIRECTORY`, @std::path::PathBuf, clap default `/tmp/package`.
  @Parameters.script_dir — `-s` / `--script-dir`, env `SCRIPT_DIRECTORY`, value name
    `SCRIPT_DIRECTORY`, @std::path::PathBuf, clap default `./agent/scripts`.
  @Parameters.template_dir — `-t` / `--template-dir`, env `TEMPLATE_DIRECTORY`, value
    name `TEMPLATE_DIRECTORY`, @std::path::PathBuf, clap default `./agent/templates`;
    carried also by the service twin, absent from the system lane, read by nothing in
    this Rust lane.
  @Parameters.agent_image — long-only `--agent-image`, env `AGENT_IMAGE`, value name
    `AGENT_IMAGE`, @String, clap default @common::DEFAULT_AGENT_IMAGE, i.e.
    `docker.io/sebt3/vynil-agent:0.7.7`; the other flag shared with the service twin.
  @Parameters.tag — long-only `--tag`, env `TAG`, value name `TAG`, @String, required;
    forwarded verbatim in `args`, never parsed or validated as a version here.
  @Parameters.config_dir — `-c` / `--config-dir`, env `CONFIG_DIR`, value name
    `CONFIG_DIR`, @std::path::PathBuf, clap default `.`.
  @Parameters.controller_values — long-only `--controller-values`, env
    `CONTROLLER_VALUES`, value name `CONTROLLER_VALUES`, @String, clap default the
    two-character string `{}`.
  Implicit runtime precondition: a live tokio multi-thread runtime (from @main's
    @tokio::main), because @context::set_tenant crosses state with
    @tokio::task::block_in_place; @context::init_k8s already ran in @tenant::run before
    this file is entered and is inert either way.

Returns:
  @Ok(@()) once the fixed eval snippet completes without a Rhai error — the @Dynamic
    value the snippet returns is discarded, never inspected.

Raises:
  @common::Error::KubeError from @TenantInstance::get when the API server rejects the
    lookup — missing `TenantInstance` (kube `NotFound` mapped whole, never defaulted),
    wrong namespace, Forbidden — the first fallible step; nothing was published to
    context or scripts when it fails.
  @common::Error::SerializationError from the explicit @map_err when
    @serde_json::to_value(@Parameters) fails on the derives.
  @common::Error::Core (transparent over @vynil_core::Error::RhaiError, Display
    `Rhai script error: <rhai text>`) from the `?` on @Script::eval — a parse error in
    the fixed snippet or any parse error / thrown error inside the imported `context`
    or `install` modules.
  The context-owned @panic! `cannot create the Kubernetes client: {e}` surfaces through
    @TenantInstance::get via @get_client_async when no kubeconfig or in-cluster
    configuration resolves.
  Panics from @context::set_tenant on a current-thread runtime or no runtime at all
    (contract in /common/src/context.sdd), not catchable by the parent `?` lane.

Handles:
  @Err lane owned by the caller — @tenant::run logs `Installing a package failed with:`
    followed by the error Display through @tracing::error and calls @process::exit(1);
    this file logs nothing and never exits, so a failed install leaves no status marker
    written by this lane.
  Failed lookup or failed eval after `@set_tenant` already ran — the process context
    keeps the @VynilContext::TenantInstance variant for the remaining process lifetime
    (which ends in the exit(1)).
  Already-installed instance — no branch on `status` here: a rerun refetches the CR and
    replays both Rhai modules; any idempotence is script-side.
  Absent resolver directories — the four search paths are never existence-checked at
    construction; the failure only lands later as the @common::Error::Core import error
    if no search dir holds `context.rhai` / `install.rhai`.
  Flags with no local reader (`vynil_namespace`, `tag`, `template_dir`, `agent_image`,
    `controller_values`) — their only observable use is the `args` JSON the scripts
    consume; template rendering off `template_dir` is script-side work.

Must:
  Execute these steps in this order, with nothing between them: build the interpreter,
    fetch the CR, publish context, inject `instance`, serialize and inject `args`,
    evaluate the snippet, return @Ok.
  Build the interpreter with @Script::new on exactly four resolver directories in this
    order: `{package_dir}/scripts`, `{config_dir}` (the directory itself),
    `{script_dir}/tenant`, `{script_dir}/lib` — plain string interpolation of
    @std::path::Display, so a path argument ending in `/` doubles the separator; earlier
    entries win an `import`.
  @Script::new brings the full registration set — including @tenant_rhai_register, so
    the scripts hold `get_tenant_instance`, `set_status_ready`, `get_tenant_name`,
    `get_tenant_services_names` and the whole @TenantInstance bridge — plus http, s3,
    the other two instance kinds, the jukebox and the k8s registrars.
  Fetch the CR with @TenantInstance::get taking clones of @Parameters.namespace and
    @Parameters.instance — one named-object read in the given namespace, never a list,
    watch or create; an absent instance is an @Err, not a bootstrap path.
  Publish the fetched CR twice from the fetched value and one clone: @set_tenant stores
    the clone as the process owner context, and @rhai::Scope::set_value on @Script::ctx
    moves the original into the script variable named `instance`.
  Serialize @Parameters with @serde_json::to_value and inject it through
    @Script::set_dynamic as the script variable named `args`; the JSON object carries
    the declared snake_case keys `namespace`, `instance`, `vynil_namespace`,
    `package_dir`, `script_dir`, `template_dir`, `agent_image`, `tag`, `config_dir`,
    `controller_values` — `controller_values` as a JSON string (its default renders
    `"{}"`, still a string, not an object), `agent_image` as a string and the @PathBufs
    as path text.
  Evaluate the fixed four-statement snippet, nothing configurable in it:
    `import("context") as ctx; let context = ctx::run(instance, args);
    import("install") as install; install::run(instance, context);` — `context` script
    first, its returned map becoming the `install::run` second argument; `install` runs
    second and last; the snippet's @Dynamic result is discarded by `let _ =` while a
    failed evaluation still propagates through `?`.
  Perform no cluster mutation of its own: every `status` or event write happens inside
    the Rhai modules through the registered @TenantInstance bridge; this file only
    reads the CR.
  Emit no log and no stdout/stderr.

Must not:
  Resolve the package through @JukeBox, pull an OCI artifact, or create or unpack
    anything under @Parameters.package_dir — package content must already be on disk
    when this subcommand starts.
  Render templates or apply manifests from Rust: `template_dir` reaches the scripts only
    through `args`, so reading it to steer this lane would move script work here.
  Interpret `tag` or `controller_values`, or gate on their contents.

Tasks:
  [ ] Cover all six Scenarios with tests; no test invokes this @run —
      /agent/tests/rhai_lifecycle.rs exercises only the service `context`/`install`
      Rhai modules on a mock engine; no tenant equivalent exists.
  [?] The fetched @TenantInstance spec carries `jukebox`/`category`/`package` coordinates
      naming a cluster-scoped @JukeBox, yet this namespaced lane neither resolves nor
      existence-checks it — resolution is entirely script-side. Decide whether the
      tenant install contract should pin the jukebox to one scope/guard its absence
      before handoff, or the scripts own that question.
  [?] The tenant context this lane installs activates the @VynilContext::TenantInstance
      branch of @get_labels — a per-apply cluster namespace read whose failures are
      swallowed to `""` (/common/src/context.sdd open task); confirm the install
      contract is meant to depend on that runtime tenant-label resolution.
  [?] Twin-mirrored open questions: the flag-shape drift against
      /agent/src/system/install.sdd, the required-but-unread flags, the `controller_values`
      JSON string, the discarded eval @Dynamic, the script-only idempotence, the
      `--agent-image` default pin and the @Deserialize derive with no deserialization
      site are all unresolved in ./../service/install.sdd Tasks on the byte-identical
      shared surface; keep those decisions in lockstep there rather than re-deciding here.

Done when:
  The six Scenarios hold under tests pinning resolver-path order, the ten-key `args`
    JSON with `controller_values` as a string and `template_dir`/`agent_image` present at
    their defaults, and the error-to-exit(1) lane.

Scenario: full run hands off in order
  Given all required flags supplied (by flag or env), an existing namespaced
    @TenantInstance named by @Parameters.instance, and `context.rhai` plus
    `install.rhai` resolvable under `{script_dir}/tenant`
  When @run is awaited
  Then @Script::new received the four search dirs `[package]/scripts`, `[config]`,
    `[script]/tenant`, `[script]/lib` in that order
  And before the eval, the process owner context is the tenant variant (via
    @set_tenant) and `instance` and `args` are bound
  Then the `context` module's `run` executes before the `install` module's `run`,
    receiving (`instance`, `args`), and the built `context` value is what
    `install::run` receives
  And @run returns @Ok(()) whatever the discarded @Dynamic was

Scenario: shared template flags reach scripts at their defaults
  Given a command line that sets the required flags but omits `-t`/`--template-dir` and
    `--agent-image`
  When @run serializes @Parameters into `args`
  Then the object holds exactly the ten keys `namespace`, `instance`,
    `vynil_namespace`, `package_dir`, `script_dir`, `template_dir`, `agent_image`,
    `tag`, `config_dir`, `controller_values`
  And `template_dir` is `./agent/templates`, `agent_image` is
    `docker.io/sebt3/vynil-agent:0.7.7` and `controller_values` is the JSON string `"{}"`

Scenario: missing CR fails before any handoff
  Given no @TenantInstance exists at that namespace/name — or its read is Forbidden
  When @run is awaited
  Then the @TenantInstance::get `?` returns @Err(@common::Error::KubeError)
  And @set_tenant never ran (context stays @VynilContext::None), `instance`/`args` were
    never injected and the snippet never evaluated
  And @tenant::run logs `Installing a package failed with:` carrying the KubeError text
    at @tracing::error level and exits the process 1

Scenario: missing required flag never reaches Rust logic
  Given `--namespace` omitted and `NAMESPACE` unset in the environment
  When the binary parses @Parameters
  Then clap exits with its usage error before @run starts — no interpreter, no cluster
    read, and the exit-1 install lane is never entered

Scenario: import failure after the CR is already published
  Given a valid @TenantInstance but neither `context.rhai` nor `install.rhai` present in
    any of the four resolver directories
  When @run evaluates the snippet
  Then @Script::eval returns @Err(@common::Error::Core Display-prefixed
    `Rhai script error:`)
  And the process context still holds the tenant variant when the exit(1) lane fires

Scenario: rerun over an installed instance
  Given a @TenantInstance whose `status.conditions` already carry `Ready`/`True` and
    `Installed`/`True` from a previous run
  When @run is invoked again with the same flags
  Then the CR is refetched and both modules replay from the top — this file skips
    nothing based on `status`
